hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"538","Amr ibn Uthman narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, Salih narrated to me. Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit al-Jumahi narrated to me, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no servant but that superstition will enter his heart; so when he feels that, let him say: I am the servant of Allah; what Allah wills; there is no power except through Allah; none brings good deeds except Allah, and none removes evil except Allah; I bear witness that Allah is capable of all things; then let him proceed on his way."
"539","Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Ali ibn Umar ibn Ali, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Medina and said: O company of Quraysh, you love livestock, so keep few of them, for you are the land of least rain; plow, for plowing is blessed, and place many skulls in it."
"540","Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, al-Darawardi narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad ibn Hafs, my father informed me, that he heard Umar ibn Ali ibn Husayn and Abdullah ibn Anbasah mentioning the skulls placed in crops. Umar ibn Ali ibn Husayn said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only commanded that because of the evil eye."
"541","Abu Salih narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Yazid ibn al-Simt, from al-Nu'man, from Makhul, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined Abu Hurayrah, then said: When you go forth to fight, and he mentioned things, saying: Do not burn a palm tree nor drown it, and do not harm a believer."
"542","It was narrated to me from Ibn Wahb, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman, from al-Qasim, the freedman of Abd al-Rahman, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, then he mentioned something similar, and said: Do not burn a palm tree nor drown it, do not cut a fruitful tree, do not kill an animal for which you have no need, and beware of harming the believer."
"543","Mahmud ibn Khalid narrated to us, al-Walid narrated to us, saying: Ibn Jabir said: Makhul narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And whoever among the Jews follows us has our protection, neither wronged nor aided against."
